<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    {{-- No <title> or description here on purpose. Both are owned by each page's
         useSeoMeta() call, which also derives og:* and twitter:* from the same
         two strings so they cannot drift apart.

         Hardcoding them here actively breaks that: @yield renders an EMPTY tag
         when a page supplies no section, and injectSeo skips any tag already
         declared — so `<meta name="description" content="">` shipped on every
         page that had no @section('description'), suppressing the real one.
         Emitting nothing lets useSeoMeta be the single source. --}}
    {{-- The font links and the pre-paint theme guard are deliberately NOT here.
         They live in config/ui.ts `app.head` (Stage 1), and injectConfigHeadTags
         adds them to this head, deduped on href and on inline script content.
         Re-adding them would emit a second copy on every marketing page.

         /marketing.css does stay here rather than in the global head: it defines
         :root, html, body, * and a, plus .btn / .panel / .mono / .reveal, which
         the authenticated app pages also use. Globalising it would restyle the
         app. Scoping it to this layout is what makes it safe. --}}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/marketing.css">
    @stack('styles')
  </head>
  <body>
    @include('SiteNav')
    @yield('content')
    @include('SiteFooter')
    @stack('scripts')
  </body>
</html>
